<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine VI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">771–c. 797</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine VI (771–c. 797) was Byzantine emperor from 780 to 797, at first under the regency of his mother Irene. He was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kardam">Khan Kardam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> at Markellai in 792, and his divorce and remarriage alienated the church. In 797 Irene had him blinded and took the throne herself, becoming the first woman to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in her own name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-vi.jpg" alt="Constantine VI" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: АНО &quot;Международный нумизматический клуб&quot; · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:INC-3040-r_%D0%A1%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B4._%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD_VI_%D0%B8_%D0%98%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0._793%E2%80%94979_%D0%B3%D0%B3._(%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%81).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
